### Example 2 -- Explicit fan-out with order ("each of you", uses `sequence`, completion criteria + branch point active)
User: "I need a joke from each one of you, let's start with Ember"
Agents: Sofia, Caius, Ember

This is the canonical "each of you" case. EVERY agent produces a DIFFERENT joke. That means `sequence`, NOT `chimeIns`. The conductor declares completion criteria + a branch point so the loop can verify all three actually told a joke and re-dispatch any that didn't.

```json
{
  "phase": "warming",
  "temperature": "casual",
  "userIntent": "Get a joke from each agent, starting with Ember.",
  "globalGuidance": "User wants three jokes, one from each agent, in the order they specified. Each agent tells THEIR OWN joke.",
  "primary": {
    "agentId": "<ember-participant-id>",
    "instruction": "Tell a short joke in your own voice. One joke, no preamble, no acknowledging Sofia.",
    "brevity": "short",
    "acknowledgePrior": "",
    "expectedOutput": "joke"
  },
  "sequence": [
    {"agentId": "<caius-participant-id>", "instruction": "Tell your own short joke. Don't reference Ember's.", "brevity": "short", "acknowledgePrior": "", "expectedOutput": "joke"},
    {"agentId": "<sofia-participant-id>", "instruction": "Tell your own short joke. Don't reference the others'. Speak as Sofia, not as anyone else.", "brevity": "short", "acknowledgePrior": "", "expectedOutput": "joke"}
  ],
  "chimeIns": [],
  "sessionSummary": "User asked for a joke from each of three agents; round in progress.",
  "completionCriteria": "All three agents (Ember, Caius, Sofia) have told their own joke.",
  "branchPoints": [
    {"condition": "any agent in sequence didn't actually tell a joke", "evaluateAfter": "after the chain settles, check whether each agent's response contained a joke; re-dispatch any that produced commentary instead"}
  ],
  "fitScore": 1.0,
  "turnMode": "answer",
  "handoff": true,
  "handoffFrom": "Sofia",
  "severity": "",
  "reason": "Explicit fan-out; sequence (not chime-ins) because each tells DIFFERENT content. Branch point catches any agent that comments instead of joking."
}
```

